You can iterate through a simple array using `FOREACH`:

```sql
DO
$$
DECLARE
v_array INTEGER[]:= '{1,2,3,4}';
v_i INTEGER;
BEGIN
FOREACH v_i IN ARRAY v_array LOOP
RAISE NOTICE 'Iteration # %', v_i;
END LOOP;
END
$$;
```

To work with multi-dimensional arrays, you can use the `SLICE` statement to access a specific dimension of the array:

```sql
DO
$$
DECLARE
v_array INTEGER[][]:= '{{1,2},{2,3},{3,5},{4,7}}';
v_i INTEGER[];
BEGIN
