Stuck on this. Attributes vary per product type and I was going to build an attribute table. The team is new to this stack, so readability matters.

### Answer:
```sql
ALTER TABLE products ADD COLUMN attrs jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}';
CREATE INDEX ON products USING gin (attrs jsonb_path_ops);

SELECT * FROM products WHERE attrs @> '{"color":"red"}';
```

Worth saying what this is *not*: an entity-attribute-value table. Concretely: EAV needs a self-join per attribute and loses types. `jsonb` with a GIN index keeps the containment query to one index scan.

